{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack","id":1468104,"title":"Thoughts on Quantum Attack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-17T02:05:20-08:00","id":1468104,"title":"Thoughts on Quantum Attack","content":"As part of a campaign setting I'm putting together, I've been looking at the kinds of nova that can be put together with low Quantum ratings. In doing this, I noted that one-dot Quantum Attack is actually rather under-powered for the investment.<br /> <br /> At one dot, at Quantum 1, the Quantum Attack power is <i>barely</i> better than a basic unarmed strike. It provides (rounding Quantum/2 up) a Scale 1, Enhancement 1, Close Range attack with a single dot for an extra Tag whilst costing 2 Quantum to power. Unarmed strike is the same without extra Tag. Body Modification Claws (mentioned as being <i>weaker</i> that Quantum Attack) actually adds up to the same (Unarmed strike but with Edged &amp; Brutal tag) without a Quantum cost. Admittedly, it <i><b>is</b></i> as good as a pistol if you choose the Ranged tag (and accept guns are Scale 1*)... but only as good as that, costs the Quantum to power, and pistols are ubiquitous in the Action Hero &amp; Super Hero genres.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's due to my reading that guns are Scale 2, but as a <i><b>house rule</b></i> (not arguing for official rules change here), I am considering adding 1 Enhancement (i.e. it gets 1 + Quantum/2 Enhancement instead of just Quantum/2). This makes it not quite as good as a gun, but better than a Body Mod that doesn't need Quantum to power it. What do others think?<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> <i>* As per the rulebooks, I am aware that devs have stated their intention was otherwise (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ale-2-firearms</a>).</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T04:29:30-08:00","id":1468111,"title":"","content":"Personally, Quantum Attack is not bad the way it is, basically because there is nothing really equal to compare. Sure guns are everywhere and there is Body Modification, but in practice, Quantum Attack will hardly be a single dot and will have a better enhancement, what the other options won\u2019t. Also you can pick any form of damage, what can be very useful.<br /> <br /> Second point is, all defensive powers have durability scale equal to dot rating, that is limited to quantum. It would put Quantum attack one scale above all defensive attacks.<br /> <br /> I, as a houserule, consider that Mega Might does not apply it\u2019s scale to punches, only when crunching things with pressure (smashing the object between your hands, or bending an iron bar), and a quantum attack must be used to create a \u201chigh scale punch\u201d if fits. If you don\u2019t want this rule, consider MM apply one scale below the might scale to the punch, to keep it leveled to other powers.<br /> <br /> If you are planning to use guns as scale 2 weapons, I suggest you to pick Quantum Attack at least at 3 dots, where you have scale 3 and 3 free tags and enhancement 2 (considering Q3). In fact, to make a Nova powerful enough to be street level without worrying much about guns, your nova must be all scale 3+, otherwise armed robbers will be real risk.<br /> <br /> Not all super powers must be more powerful than guns, they can be just as good as punches at distance, but, if you think it is not a big deal, increase the scale of Quantum Attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:37:03-08:00","id":1468160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468111#post1468111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, Quantum Attack is not bad the way it is, basically because there is nothing really equal to compare. Sure guns are everywhere and there is Body Modification, but <b>in practice, Quantum Attack will hardly be a single dot and will have a better enhancement</b>, what the other options won\u2019t. Also you can pick any form of damage, what can be very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Eterni Knight is looking at Quantum Attack from the point of view of being purchased on a Quantum 1 nova which means it would be limited to one dot. <br /> <br /> Despite it possibly being a bit under-powered at that level, it does still have some things going for it... it cannot be disarmed like a gun it can potentially originate from various places allowing use in some cases that claws of a gun wouldn't be useable and can be defined as a variety of themes/effects that might interact differently with targets than a mere gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:50:57-08:00","id":1468164,"title":"","content":"Also, its \u201cammo\u201d is extremely easy to come by; just wait a bit until your quantum reserve replenishes. And if you really, truly need more power, you can always max out \u2014 something that I wouldn't allow for body modification without a very good explanation, let alone handguns. (I think that it is technically possible to max out on mega edges; but they strike me as something that aren't always suitable for maxing out, conceptually.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T12:12:06-08:00","id":1468167,"title":"","content":"Well, a Quantum 1 nova is not that powerful, they have powers but the powers are all same scale as humans (except mega attributes), so it\u2019s not that the Nova is going to weak in one aspect because they have just one dot in Quantum Attack, the nova will be basically a normal person that have some powers, that are not different from basic tech (or even weaker). The powers are more about flash and cosmetic and less about raw power.<br /> <br /> The same rules applies to Toughness, why not give scale to the armor? The armor will be equivalent to a let her armor, just a bit more versatile because it protects against all kinds of damage, not just stabbing or bullets or what ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T14:51:02-08:00","id":1468181,"title":"","content":"Quantum Attack wouldn't be the only power that isn't worth it at 1 dot; Boost is a complete waste of points until you get at least 2 levels and an Extra Attribute Tag, while 1 dot in Quantum Agent gets you a mostly useless minion. I presume the intent is that you build the power into something useful over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T16:49:15-08:00","id":1468194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468111#post1468111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but in practice, Quantum Attack will hardly be a single dot...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brennanhawkwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468160#post1468160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eterni Knight is looking at Quantum Attack from the point of view of being purchased on a Quantum 1 nova which means it would be limited to one dot.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack#post1468104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking at the kinds of nova that can be put together with low Quantum ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is all coming from the perspective of low-powered novas. Single dot of Quantum. So Max of one dot in any power.<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e\u200f\u200f\u200e<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468111#post1468111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you can pick any form of damage, what can be very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468164#post1468164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you really, truly need more power, you can always max out...</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't consider, but you're right - these do actually beef up a Quantum Attack power. A &quot;flame breath&quot; power that can not on set things on fire, but be &quot;pushed&quot; to hitting at Scale 2 is powerful &amp; flexible. I honestly didn't think of the damage form &amp; maxing out at low levels. My mind was stuck at the &quot;pure&quot; stats, not what it can be pushed to creatively by players (or explicitly with the &quot;max out&quot; feature).<br /> <br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468111#post1468111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second point is, all defensive powers have durability scale equal to dot rating, that is limited to quantum. It would put Quantum attack one scale above all defensive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't suggesting a Scale increase? Merely a single extra dot of enhancement. So it won't effect anything with Durability 4, can't cause an extra Inflict Damage stunt, etc. However, I am rethinking this given the above. A little &quot;effort&quot; and they CAN make it as good as a Scale 2 gun (with two dots of Tags). So yeah, reconsidering the enhancement.<br /> <br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468111#post1468111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are planning to use guns as scale 2 weapons, I suggest you to pick Quantum Attack at least at 3 dots, where you have scale 3 and 3 free tags and enhancement 2 (considering Q3). In fact, to make a Nova powerful enough to be street level without worrying much about guns, your nova must be all scale 3+, otherwise armed robbers will be real risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the feeling from the comments in the book that &quot;stealth novas&quot; were definitely meant to be at or above <i>street level</i>. Then again, &quot;street level&quot; can mean very different things to different people. Even in the same universe, street level heroes can be everything from Jessica Jones &amp; Daredevil depicted on TV as vulnerable to guns (should someone actually manage to land a shot) to Luke Cage who is bullet-proof and needs specialised Scale 3+ guns to harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26905,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","user":"Eternl Knight","date":".  Clarity. 11-17-2021, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:07:26-08:00","id":1468197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468167#post1468167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a Quantum 1 nova is not that powerful...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468181#post1468181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantum Attack wouldn't be the only power that isn't worth it at 1 dot...</div> </div> </div> </div>This does seem to be what I'm taking away from this. But I think I might be OK with that. One dot of Mega-Attribute and/or Powers that <i><b>need</b></i> to be maxed out to be noticeably more than human. Someone that can hit hard &quot;enough&quot; and take &quot;enough&quot; of a punch to feel like a Talent focused on being tough/strong but coming from the basis of being a very low-end super instead of a super-skilled, lucky action hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468167#post1468167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same rules applies to Toughness, why not give scale to the armor? The armor will be equivalent to a let her armor, just a bit more versatile because it protects against all kinds of damage, not just stabbing or bullets or what ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you're going with here. I think Q1 offence &amp; defence should be Scale 1. think it makes a bit of sense, but thought that the powers were a little &quot;under-powered&quot; as written for their cost. I hadn't taken into account the &quot;max out&quot; potential though. With the flexibility of the damage form, I think that gives Q1 characters the potential to be tougher/stronger with the potential to level up their offence/defence during times of stress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26905,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","user":"Eternl Knight","date":".  Forgot closing tag 11-17-2021, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T17:11:10-08:00","id":1468200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468197#post1468197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does seem to be what I'm taking away from this. But I think I might be OK with that. One dot of Mega-Attribute and/or Powers that <i><b>need</b></i> to be maxed out to be noticeably more than human. Someone that can hit hard &quot;enough&quot; and take &quot;enough&quot; of a punch to feel like a Talent focused on being tough/strong but coming from the basis of being a very low-end super instead of a super-skilled, lucky action hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want them to feel like a Talent, you may want to wait until Adventure! is published, since Stalwarts are designed using the Talent ruleset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T18:53:42-08:00","id":1468210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468200#post1468200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want them to feel like a Talent, you may want to wait until Adventure! is published, since Stalwarts are designed using the Talent ruleset.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thought has crossed my mind, but I'm trying to minimise the rulesets needed to play in the setting. That and I'd have to wait until I can buy the PDF from DriveThruRPG and I'm trying to get this done before Christmas when I have the time to run the game for my boys. Hard to get time with my sons as life gets busier for all of us again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T19:25:30-08:00","id":1468211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468210#post1468210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought has crossed my mind, but I'm trying to minimise the rulesets needed to play in the setting. That and I'd have to wait until I can buy the PDF from DriveThruRPG and I'm trying to get this done before Christmas when I have the time to run the game for my boys. Hard to get time with my sons as life gets busier for all of us again.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're limiting the game to Quantum 1, I can see five potential problems you may not have considered:<br /> <br /> 1). If my quick flip through the book was right, 18 of the 32 powers (not Mega-Edges or Mega-Attributes) need Q2-Q4 to take them. That's over half.<br /> 2). Many dice pools are Quantum + Power, which means they'd be rolling 2 dice and failing a lot.<br /> 3). Maxing Out is unlikely to work when you're only rolling 1 die. Frequent failures are frustrating.<br /> 4). Q1 = 15 quantum points. If they have powers that require quantum points, they could run out fast, which would also be frustrating.<br /> 5). You can't take more points in a single Tag than you have dots in the power. This is very limiting if you only have one dot in the power.<br /> <br /> My off-the-cuff solution would be:<br /> 1). Let them buy up to Quantum 5. This does a lot to solve issues 1-4 while giving them something to spend starting xp on instead of 12 different powers.<br /> 2). Let them take 2+ levels in specific Tags with Storyguide approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 11-17-2021, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T19:44:00-08:00","id":1468214,"title":"","content":"While I agree with the list Shepherdboi made, there are a few observations worth to mention.<br /> <br /> 1. The powers out of reach of a Q1 Nova will hardly be missed in a Pulp-ish game, as they are more super heroic and less pulpy.<br /> 2. Most of the powers that you can buy with Q1 need no Q+P rolls (worth to check, but I have a Q3 cap game to be played and went after it)<br /> 3. Maxing out will be really difficult, it will be the best momentum drain in the game for sure.<br /> 4.That is true, you will need to keep an eye on it and worth to point the players in the direction of Mega Attributes and Edges. Also the Quantum generating powers will be out of reach (absorption and quantum leech).<br /> 5. The best tags for a low quantum nova will be out of reach (reduced cost by far).<br /> <br /> On your solutions<br /> 1. it would change a lot the feeling of the game. A Q1 game is very much human, while a Q5 is very powerful in huge scales. if you try to keep the cap around 2-3 it will have a balance (I like the Q3 cap, allowing to pick Q4-5 powers if you have Q3)<br /> 2. Maybe worth, but not sure if it will change much of the player options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T20:13:59-08:00","id":1468217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468214#post1468214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. it would change a lot the feeling of the game. A Q1 game is very much human, while a Q5 is very powerful in huge scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The difference between a Q1 nova with 1 dot powers and a Q5 nova with 1 dot powers is that the Q5 nova tends to succeed more consistently and last longer before running out of energy. There is no huge power difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T21:50:40-08:00","id":1468225,"title":"","content":"OK, to give context, the idea for my campaign setting is based on 'The Boys' (comic as I've not seen the TV series). In that universe, the source of powers is a chemical agent that costs unfathomable amounts to make in a pure form and the younger a person is given a dose, the more powerful they are. The world's Superman analog needed to be given a one or more large, pure doses of the chemical agent in his infancy. Large doses (of varying purity) in childhood is pretty much a requirement to get powers recognisable as &quot;super&quot; (and come with the complication the world's Evil Corp pretty much owns you afterward). Get dosed as an adult, even with the high quality / pure stuff, results in being tougher, stronger, and perhaps a bit faster than baselines... but to (at best) Captain America levels.<br /> <br /> For my purposes, the players will be taking on the role of plucky heroes taking it on themselves to deal with supers that get protected by the evil &quot;Super Heroes Inc&quot; corporation. They'd either be Talents picked for their outstanding (but still &quot;human&quot; capabilities) or they'd be 'baselines' affected in some life-altering bad way by supers who get given a dose of the super-power catalyst as an adult, getting low level super powers.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I had been thinking about keeping Quantum capped at 1 to reflect their &quot;low level&quot; powers, but as I'm working it through, I'm finding that low-level novas in the current rules are very underpowered compared to low-level novas in the Aberrant of my childhood. A Quantum 1 &quot;old school&quot; nova with Quantum Bolt 1 in the old rules was working with the equivalent of an SMG or Heavy Pistol. A Quantum 1 with Quantum Attack 1 &quot;new school&quot; nova is just throwing the equivalent of a ranged punch.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> - What does your Q3-cap feel like in practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T01:09:55-08:00","id":1468244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468217#post1468217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. The difference between a Q1 nova with 1 dot powers and a Q5 nova with 1 dot powers is that the Q5 nova tends to succeed more consistently and last longer before running out of energy. There is no huge power difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Q5 Nova with no Scale 5 powers made really bad choices in their XP use. I mean, if you have Quantum 5 and Quantum attack 1, you gain 2e in the attack, but lose the chance to destroy warships with your attack. There are those cases, sure, but usually when we talk Q5 we are talking about Scale 5 powers, basically optimized XP spending.<br /> <br /> Now on Q3 feeling in practice, I have had the chance to run a game where most players were Q2-3, with a single Q4 and the the Q4 was afraid of his powers (he thinks he killed people when erupted). The general feeling was interesting, we didn\u2019t use that much of scale, the game was a lot of investigation with a few combat scenes, but was fun, with no cases of Collateral damages (and I tracked it per session). The climax was a fight against a Nova inventor that had Durability scale enough to be completely immune to all their attacks (6 if I am not wrong) and a serious mental unbalance that compelled him to invent stuff, basically supplying gangs all over the city with Nova tech just to get more money to invent more stuff, but no intention to harm anyone.<br /> <br /> My idea for Q3 cap is to keep it on reasonable scale, like you can take a tank cannon shot in your chest, but it will hurt as hell, and you can attack it back, but it\u2019s not going to be with a single attack that you will destroy it. If you max out you could do some collateral damage, but not level a city by mistake.<br /> <br /> On the idea of a The Boys like game, instead of Q1, use Talents. You have no idea what they can do until you use talents in your game. They are more flexible than Q1 Novas and may have the feeling of low level super powers without the flash part. Talents can for example spend inspiration for scale, and with a gift ignore scale differences, what means their attacks gain scale against high scale targets, but it will happen just once in a while (2 times per scene, possibly), not all the time like novas. And they could gain a lot of advantages with some Novatech, if available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T04:28:25-08:00","id":1468253,"title":"","content":"Just a little observation: we have to remember that powers, in RPGs, are not only about mechanical advantages. Their first benefit is what I call &quot;Narrative Permission&quot; - that is, you couldn't try to do something, but if you have this power/advantage/whatever, now you can.<br /> <br /> So, even if a Quantum Attack is weaker than a gun, it does allow me to enter somewhere unarmed, even naked, and even then, have the Narrative Permission to do something that only an armed person normally could.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't you love to have the &quot;Narrative Permission&quot; to levitate, in the real world? Even if it was in Speed Scale &quot;0.001&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 11-18-2021, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T05:29:16-08:00","id":1468258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468225#post1468225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, I had been thinking about keeping Quantum capped at 1 to reflect their &quot;low level&quot; powers, but as I'm working it through, I'm finding that low-level novas in the current rules are very underpowered compared to low-level novas in the Aberrant of my childhood. A Quantum 1 &quot;old school&quot; nova with Quantum Bolt 1 in the old rules was working with the equivalent of an SMG or Heavy Pistol. A Quantum 1 with Quantum Attack 1 &quot;new school&quot; nova is just throwing the equivalent of a ranged punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, yeah, the system is different than original Aberrant. Then you could buy 5 dots in powers as long as you meant the Quantum minimum. In TC:Aberrant, you are always capped by your Quantum. I'd say you're describing something around scale 2 or 3 generally for powers. Which means you're looking at a cap of 2 or 3 on your Quantum. However, if you're willing to homebrew, what you're describing also sounds like a Mite user. There are no rules around Mite in TC:Aberrant right now, but I could see your players juicing up before facing someone. Depends on how dark a tone you want. I'll also suggest you look into the Tone and Subgenre section of the book and see if any of the rules there tickle your fancy for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T06:44:26-08:00","id":1468265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468258#post1468258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then you could buy 5 dots in powers as long as you met the Quantum minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still true!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468258#post1468258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In TC:Aberrant, you are always capped by your Quantum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you see this? This is only true in powers that the Quantum Minimum says &quot;Quantum Minimum = Dots&quot; or &quot;Quantum Minimum = Dots +x&quot; or something like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T07:04:08-08:00","id":1468266,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I thought they all said Quantum Minimum = Dots or Dots + X. It's been awhile since I built characters in the game. Looking through, about 1/3 to 1/2 of the powers can be bought with dots above Quantum. So that's cooler than I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T14:01:34-08:00","id":1468299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468244#post1468244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a Q5 Nova with no Scale 5 powers made really bad choices in their XP use. I mean, if you have Quantum 5 and Quantum attack 1, you gain 2e in the attack, but lose the chance to destroy warships with your attack. There are those cases, sure, but usually when we talk Q5 we are talking about Scale 5 powers, basically optimized XP spending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually, yes, but that isn't applicable here since the OP specified they were looking to run a campaign limited to 1 dot powers. In this case, Quantum 5 isn't meant to provide massive cosmic power, but to provide fuel and consistent success with a bunch of weak powers.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I've always assumed you should pump Quantum as high as your Storyguide allows at character creation, no matter how many points you put into your actual powers. After all, improving a power requires you to Max Out that power once, but improving your Quantum rating involves Maxing Out your Quantum rating a number of times equal to your current Quantum rating. So taking a power from 1 dot to 5 dots requires Maxing Out the power four times, but taking your Quantum rating from 1 dot to 5 dots requires Maxing Out your Quantum rating ten times; which is harder than it seems since players are more likely to spend Maxing Out successes on actual powers rather than Quantum. Starting at Quantum 4 or 5 bypasses that training time, and gives you a bigger Maxing Out pool to boot, meaning you gain new nova traits faster and with less Flux. Successfully Maxing Out during combat is also fun and dramatic, which is always important during a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T20:40:53-08:00","id":1468327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468253#post1468253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a little observation: we have to remember that powers, in RPGs, are not only about mechanical advantages. Their first benefit is what I call &quot;Narrative Permission&quot; - that is, you couldn't try to do something, but if you have this power/advantage/whatever, now you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's actually part of the reason I want to mix Talents with low-powered Novas. The difference between &quot;lucky/skilled action hero&quot; and &quot;low powered super&quot; is precisely what I'm looking for in giving the players different &quot;Narrative Permissions&quot; at the table.<br /> <br /> My son playing an action hero, through their Inspiration &amp; Dramatic Editing, gets to be Jason Bourne when it comes to car chases &amp; evading security, John McClane when it comes to shooting things to make them explode, and John Wick when it comes to knowing the right people &amp; convincing them to help him. My son playing a low-powered super, through his low-level powers &amp; maxing out, gets to be Luke Cage tanking a knife to the chest, Peter Parker dodging a hailstorm of bullets, and Jessica Jones throwing a car into a bunch of Russian Mafia goons.<br /> <br /> It's a halfway point between the flexibility of &quot;anyone can do everything&quot; and the stifling restrictions of classes in D&amp;D. The Talents push themselves to stunts within the realm of physics with skill/luck that boggles the mind, the low-level Novas push themselves beyond the bounds of physics but without the class or skill the Talents can pull out of nowhere.<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468258#post1468258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, the system is different than original Aberrant. ... I'd say you're describing something around scale 2 or 3 generally for powers. Which means you're looking at a cap of 2 or 3 on your Quantum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm coming to that conclusion myself. Thinking I might cap Quantum &amp; Powers at 3, with some limitations on what their powers can be / look like (to fit the theme, they don't get the flashy powers - they're more Luke Cage, Mother's Milk, &amp; Matt Murdoch than the X-Men).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468258#post1468258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if you're willing to homebrew, what you're describing also sounds like a Mite user. There are no rules around Mite in TC:Aberrant right now, but I could see your players juicing up before facing someone. Depends on how dark a tone you want. I'll also suggest you look into the Tone and Subgenre section of the book and see if any of the rules there tickle your fancy for your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking about having weak/impure doses of the catalyst available in the world and coming up with a temporary Mega-Might/Mega-Stamina dots (based on dosage) but coming with an &quot;Addiction&quot; complication and/or post-high &quot;Comedown&quot; complication (both with effects scaling by dosage).<br /> <br /> That said, I do like the idea of allowing each character <i>template</i> have their own area of specialty. Talents are the kings &amp; queens of pulling off a wide range of physically/intellectually <i>implausible</i> stunts as needed whereas Novas (even low-level ones) pull off the physically <i>impossible</i> but in ways that can more easily be predicted/countered once you accept what it is they can do (Luke Cage can tank a bullet and lift a car... but he's not walking into Monte Carlo, embarrassing an international super-villain at their chosen game of cards, then turning their partner into an ally like James Bond).<br /> <br /> Thanks for the suggestion on the Tone/Subgenre sections. Already looking into them and will be picking a few extra mechanics out of them to better represent the nature of the game (will have a big post on that once we get through our first session).<br /> <br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<br /> \u200f\u200f\u200e \u200e<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468104-thoughts-on-quantum-attack?p=1468299#post1468299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually, yes, but that isn't applicable here since the OP specified they were looking to run a campaign limited to 1 dot powers. In this case, Quantum 5 isn't meant to provide massive cosmic power, but to provide fuel and consistent success with a bunch of weak powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is indeed the case. Whilst I understand the arguments when it comes to min-maxing Quantum to match the powers you plan to use (and you are both making reasonable points for optimising a build) - I don't want people able to cut through a warship. They're low-power supers. The high-power supers are the antagonists (at least for the initial games, I have hazy plans about running a supers game in the same universe with the old characters playing the part of team nemeses).<br /> <br /> I think I'll be taking advice from both of you. I'll bump up the powers cap to 2 (with an optional single &quot;stand-out&quot; power at 3 if desired), bump the Quantum cap to 3, and make a few characters within those bounds to see how it works. Quantum 2/3, with the Momentum pool, should give a reasonable chance of at least one success at &quot;maxing out&quot; when needed, with enough fuel &amp; dice to pull off what they need to with the powers. A max of Quantum 3 means they can be &quot;resistant&quot; to Scale 2 firearms (yes, sticking with that) if they want to be without being immune to gunfire, punch through a brick wall but not (easily) through reinforced steel, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}